# Catatan deploy STB (family-mcp)

When a change to `family-mcp` is ready for the STB server, add a release note in
the same change. Ritual: `deploy/README.md`. Template:
`deploy/releases/_template.md`.

## When to write one

Write `deploy/releases/pending/YYYY-MM-DD-nama-fitur.md` (today's date) when the
work changes what STB runs: MCP tool behavior, calls to the FamilyRoots API, env,
Dockerfile, or dependencies.

Skip it for docs-only edits and refactors with no runtime change.

## What to put in it

Copy the template. Keep all four sections. Write **Tidak ada.** when a section
does not apply.

- **Env** — list new keys and why. Add the same keys to `.env.example` and
  `.env.docker.example`. Do not put secret values in the note.
- **Build** — Dockerfile, base image, or dependency changes.
  `scripts/deploy.sh` always rebuilds the image.
- **Data awal** — service ini tidak punya database atau seeder. Hampir selalu
  `Tidak ada.`
- **Cek setelah naik** — one command per bash fence. The deploy script runs each
  fence as one command. A `curl` fails on connection error, HTTP 404, or HTTP
  5xx. Any other command fails on a non-zero exit code. The MCP port is usually
  not published to the host, so use
  `docker compose --env-file .env.docker exec -T family-mcp ...`.

Do not put deploy notes in `docs/`.

## Do not mark shipped

Leave the new note in `pending/`. `scripts/deploy.sh` moves every pending note
to `shipped/` after those checks pass. Do not `git mv` it yourself while
implementing the change.
